;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "Graham_Hutton-Programming_in_Haskell-Cambridge_University_Press(2007)"
 :source "Haskell/other downloaded books/Haskell/Graham_Hutton-Programming_in_Haskell-Cambridge_University_Press(2007).pdf"
 :page 19
 :exercises "Headings a book with no outline sets by glyph size alone.  The
chapter opener is an eyebrow pair - Chapter 2 at 1.84 body heights over
First Steps at 2.21 - and each section heading arrives as two blocks,
the number (2.1) split from its title (The Hugs system) at the same
baseline, both at 1.28.  The old text-only synthesis promoted none of
them: the split number has no capital after it and the titles carry no
number.  The geometry synthesis must merge each pair and promote the
merged block - the eyebrow at cluster rank, the sections at dot depth."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0))
